        </templateparamlist>
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void BlockingPool&lt; T &gt;::forEachIdle</definition>
        <argsstring>(Func &amp;&amp;func, Finish &amp;&amp;finish)</argsstring>
        <name>forEachIdle</name>
        <qualifiedname>BlockingPool::forEachIdle</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>Func &amp;&amp;</type>
          <declname>func</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>Finish &amp;&amp;</type>
          <declname>finish</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classVisits" kindref="compound">Visits</ref> every idle item with <computeroutput>func</computeroutput>, then calls <computeroutput>finish</computeroutput>, under the pool lock. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Holding the lock across both callbacks prevents <ref refid="classBlockingPool_1aa577bb9f7274c91f2ba9912cac021769" kindref="member">acquire()</ref> from handing out an item while it is being operated on (e.g. reconnected) or before the follow-up work in <computeroutput>finish</computeroutput> has completed. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Func</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callable taking <computeroutput>std::shared_ptr&lt;T&gt;&amp;</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Finish</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callable invoked once after all items were visited. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">func</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Per-item operation. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">finish</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Final operation, typically waiting for async work started by func. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Keeping <computeroutput>finish</computeroutput> inside the lock is intentional; a callback that tries to acquire from the same pool would deadlock. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
