    <briefdescription>
<para>Thread-safe fixed set of reusable items leased one caller at a time. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Items are added with <ref refid="classBlockingPool_1ab15e0709ecb1d8979957d54b2e666f78" kindref="member">release()</ref> and leased with <ref refid="classBlockingPool_1aa577bb9f7274c91f2ba9912cac021769" kindref="member">acquire()</ref>, which waits up to a timeout and returns <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> if nothing becomes free. The pool is independent of the database so it can be unit tested with plain objects. Used by <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool" kindref="compound">DatabaseConnectionPool</ref> to hand out <ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref> connections; <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref> models the matching RAII lease. <verbatim>     Thread-safety: a single mutex protects the deque, a condition
</verbatim> variable wakes waiting acquirers, and all methods may be called concurrently. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the pooled items (held via <computeroutput>std::shared_ptr</computeroutput>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
